.TH manualtoolchange_ui "1" "2026-08-03" "LinuxCNC Documentation" "The Enhanced Machine Controller"
.SH NAME
manualtoolchange_ui \- manual tool change prompt window

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B manualtoolchange_ui

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B manualtoolchange_ui
shows the operator prompt for manual tool changes.  It connects to the
.B manualtoolchange
component in
.BR stmakd (1)
over the REST API, polls for a pending tool change request, and pops up
a dialog asking the operator to insert (or remove) the tool and click
Continue, which confirms the change to the controller.  It replaces the
.B hal_manualtoolchange
user interface of earlier LinuxCNC releases, which used HAL pins
directly.
.PP
It takes no command-line arguments and is normally started by the
machine configuration, not by hand.  The window withdraws itself after
a few seconds and reappears when a tool change is requested; it is safe
to close or iconify it.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B STMAK_REST_URL
Base URL of the stmakd REST interface (default
.BR http://127.0.0.1:5080 ).
.TP
.B STMAK_MTC_INSTANCE
Name of the manualtoolchange component instance to talk to (default
.BR manualtoolchange ).

.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR stmakd (1),
.BR axis (1)

